On 3/19/07, Karl Naylor <karl.org@gmail.com> wrote:
> On 19/03/07, Turniansky, Michael <MICHAEL.A.TURNIANSKY@saic.com> wrote:

> > > .i zo'o mi dapma le rodo ka tolcando
> >   Ungrammatical.  You want either .i zo'o mi dapma le le rodo ka
> > tolcando

> My reasoning was that {do} does not take an article, as it is a
> pro-sumti.

{le do ka tolcando} would have been fine. The problem is that the sumti
in the LE <sumti> <selbri> construction cannot have an outer quantifier.

{le ro do} is also a valid sumti without outer quantifier, so
Michael's suggestion
also works.

> Alternatively, what about "le ka tolcando pe rodo"?

Yes, and {le pe ro do ka tolcando} is yet another possibility.

